{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/llng8c","slideIndex":0,"text":"Research question and evaluation aims for the present study. These are questions rather than established results. Predict means estimating human finger aperture from the measured hand–object distance. Function approximation uses the current distance. MLP uses five frames of distance history. LSTM uses full available distance history. Compare performance separately across 20, 30 and 40 mm objects. Prosthetic actuation remains future work."}